1
00:00:21,119 --> 00:00:24,880
Iowa, we have done it.

2
00:00:26,510 --> 00:00:28,830
What they said was impossible.

3
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:34,830
Together, Iowa, we have proven that the impossible was possible.

4
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:47,150
And as we said in the primary, and I'll say it again, Iowa, you sure do love an underdog.

5
00:00:47,160 --> 00:01:03,200
After 448 days of hard work, pushing up hills, knocking doors, visiting all 99 counties, visiting small and midsize communities all across this state,

6
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,720
And preaching the message of a better future for Iowa.

7
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:10,780
Together, we have made history.

8
00:01:11,260 --> 00:01:24,100
For the first time in 20 years, Iowa will have representation in the United States Senate for the people of Iowa.

9
00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:33,310
As I have said all along, my story is truly the American dream.

10
00:01:34,130 --> 00:01:44,950
Only in America could someone born into a working-class family in Council Bluffs, Iowa, who went through the economic and health care struggle that I went through ultimately be able to represent

11
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:53,690
My country in four Paralympic games, win two gold medals, represent my community in the Iowa legislature, and as of tonight,

12
00:01:54,150 --> 00:02:00,990
Be elected to represent the state I was born and raised in in the United States Senate.

13
00:02:03,870 --> 00:02:06,531
Only in America is this possible.

14
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:16,910
And as your next United States Senator, Iowa, I promise to protect the American dream for future generations.

15
00:02:17,850 --> 00:02:23,610
I just got off the phone with Ashley Hinson and commended her on running a strong campaign.

16
00:02:23,610 --> 00:02:26,110
Campaigns, they are brutal.

17
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:29,670
I wish her and her family all the best.

18
00:02:29,670 --> 00:02:33,250
I have deep respect for anyone who steps up to run.

19
00:02:33,370 --> 00:02:34,270
Yeah, it's worth it.

20
00:02:34,370 --> 00:02:35,010
Give her a clap.

21
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:41,320
I appreciate her service to Iowa for the last few years.

22
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:51,680
Our campaign finance system is broken and nasty campaign commercials bought by billionaires trying to buy off our elections make it even worse.

23
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:56,640
But tonight, Iowa, we outvoted the billionaires.

24
00:02:56,640 --> 00:03:10,420
We outworked the corporate PACs, and we told every single corrupt politician, enough is enough.

25
00:03:15,470 --> 00:03:17,690
Here's my promise to each and every one of you.

26
00:03:17,910 --> 00:03:24,572
First and foremost, in the United States Senate, I will fight to end this war in Iran.

27
00:03:26,420 --> 00:03:34,820
Yes, I will fight to end these chaotic tariffs because they are decimating markets, killing farmers, and hurting our rural communities.

28
00:03:36,152 --> 00:03:45,242
I am going to the U.S. Senate to fight for a livable wage, because $7.25 is not a livable wage for Iowans.

29
00:03:45,242 --> 00:03:52,760
I am going to the Senate to fight for affordable housing, to drive private equity out of housing,

30
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:54,480
Out of healthcare, and out of nursing homes.

31
00:03:57,210 --> 00:04:12,510
I'm going up there to fight for affordable and accessible health care because I believe that health care is a human right and a part of that human right is also women's Reproductive freedom.

32
00:04:15,849 --> 00:04:27,210
I'm also going up to the US Senate to fight for affordable and accessible prescription drugs because far too often as I've traveled this state I've heard over and over this month

33
00:04:27,210 --> 00:04:33,310
It's either taking my pills or paying my bills that is wrong in the richest country on earth.

34
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:44,280
And I'm going to the US Senate to fight for our public schools because I believe public money belongs in our public schools.

35
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:56,915
I am going up to the United States Senate to pass a farm bill and a farm bill for small family farmers in rural communities,

36
00:04:56,915 --> 00:04:57,690
Not just Big Ag.

37
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:08,760
And I am going to fight and address the cancer crisis because it is wrong that Iowa leads the nation in cancer.

38
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:16,200
And I'm going to fight to address the root cause of that cancer crisis, which is our water quality crisis.

39
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:21,760
Every Iowan deserves when they turn on their tap to ensure that their water is not giving them cancer.

40
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:34,240
And maybe most importantly, I am going up to DC to end the corruption that we are seeing on both sides of the aisle.

41
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:41,590
We need to have campaign finance reform.

42
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:56,360
And I am going to DC to overturn Citizens United because in Iowa, Elon Musk does not decide our elections.

43
00:05:57,300 --> 00:06:00,115
Iowans do and we proved it tonight.

44
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:10,900
I also want to fight for ethics reforms, term limits, banning members of Congress from owning and trading stocks.

45
00:06:11,340 --> 00:06:20,280
And I want to pass a bill to mandate members of Congress to have at least one in-person town hall annually because members of Congress should be accountable to the people,

46
00:06:20,580 --> 00:06:23,560
To the constituents, not just to their donors and lobbyists.

47
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:26,360
This is what I'm going to the United States Senate to fight for.

48
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:27,340
All of you.

49
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:43,100
15 months ago, we launched this campaign because we believed that Iowa deserved representation in the Senate, a senator who works for the people of Iowa.

50
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:45,120
So, we began our push for change.

51
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:48,420
The beginning of this, they said we were crazy.

52
00:06:49,280 --> 00:06:53,900
They said winning a state that Trump had won by 13 points was impossible.

53
00:06:54,780 --> 00:07:01,400
That running against someone like Ashley Hinson with her corporate PAC friends and super PAC allies was impossible.

54
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:04,660
But I've heard the impossible my whole life.

55
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:11,660
Doctors told me and my parents it was impossible for me to live a fulfilled life after I was born with spina bifida.

56
00:07:12,430 --> 00:07:13,830
Proved them wrong then.

57
00:07:13,830 --> 00:07:19,580
They told me it was impossible to win gold medals after I was cut from the US national team six straight times.

58
00:07:20,105 --> 00:07:23,350
Proved them wrong then.

59
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:28,070
They told me it was impossible to win my western Iowa district as a Democrat.

60
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:30,118
Well, we proved them wrong then.

61
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:35,760
And they told me it was impossible to win this Senate race.

62
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:41,220
But tonight, Iowa, we have once again proved that the impossible is possible.

63
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:55,600
I spent the last 448 days crisscrossing this beautiful state, going to all 99 counties, urban areas, rural areas,

64
00:07:56,100 --> 00:08:06,900
NASCAR tracks, county fairs, RAGBRAI, tailgates, small family farms, health clinics, rural pharmacies, meeting people wherever they are.

65
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:10,420
And wherever I went, I heard the same thing.

66
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:16,580
They would say, "Josh, I'm struggling just to keep food on the table, keep a roof above my head,

67
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:21,880
Pay my electric bill, and with this war in Iran, I'm struggling just to keep gas in my tank."

68
00:08:22,820 --> 00:08:25,740
Over those 448 days, I heard a lot of hurting.

69
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:28,220
But I also heard a lot of hope.

70
00:08:28,220 --> 00:08:30,680
Hope that change was coming.

71
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:39,300
Hope that we'd find our way back to the Iowa I grew up in, where you could afford to go to your doctor and where you were proud to send your kids

72
00:08:39,300 --> 00:08:41,740
To some of the nation's best public schools.

73
00:08:42,626 --> 00:08:45,300
And tonight, we have done it.

74
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:54,580
All along I have said that Iowa was the center of the political universe.

75
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:56,940
And man, did we prove that true tonight.

76
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:13,580
Not only our victory here tonight, but Rob's victory, Sarah's victory, Lindsay's victory, Christina's victory that has been made crystal clear.

77
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:16,120
We have changed the state of Iowa tonight.

78
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:22,460
Rob Sand is going to be a tremendous governor.

79
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:27,320
He will undo the privatization of Medicaid and strengthen our public schools.

80
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:34,180
So every Iowan has the opportunity to receive a world-class education right here in Iowa.

81
00:09:37,820 --> 00:09:43,660
And I am so excited to join these three amazing women, Lindsay, Christina, and Sarah.

82
00:09:43,940 --> 00:09:49,320
They will be excellent representation who will fight for the people of Iowa.

83
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:58,310
And I look forward to serving alongside these amazing women to fight for Iowans.

84
00:09:58,310 --> 00:10:01,640
So now Iowa, let us be the city on a hill.

85
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:05,760
The Iowa that we grew up in that was the envy of the nation.

86
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:13,780
Where a mom and a dad don't have to work two to three jobs just to keep food on the table and gas in the tank.

87
00:10:14,500 --> 00:10:18,960
Where our farmers can afford to keep working the land their grandfathers did.

88
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:24,499
And where every Iowa child has access to world-class education.

89
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:27,668
Where we fix our broken health care system.

90
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:35,600
So where you live doesn't determine if you live, where our young people want to and can afford to stay in Iowa,

91
00:10:36,060 --> 00:10:38,880
Have a family, buy a house, and start a life.

92
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:43,040
Iowa, this is where our comeback begins.

93
00:10:48,170 --> 00:10:49,610
Let us do it together.

94
00:10:50,190 --> 00:10:58,366
Like what Abraham Lincoln said, guided by the better angels of our nature and do what is right for Iowa and Iowans.

95
00:10:58,730 --> 00:11:05,990
Whether you voted for me today or not, I will always fight for Iowa and Iowans and I pledge to be a senator for all of you,

96
00:11:06,370 --> 00:11:08,130
Regardless of political affiliation.

97
00:11:08,130 --> 00:11:14,890
My political North Star has always been about what is best for the people, not about party.

98
00:11:15,630 --> 00:11:20,290
What is best for our working families, our small family farms, and our small businesses.

99
00:11:21,370 --> 00:11:25,070
And I will always be accountable to you, the people.

100
00:11:29,689 --> 00:11:41,460
Since I began this, I've been saying that it's going to be something beautifully poetic that the man who is coming to get Senator Harkin's seat back is only there because of

101
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:43,740
The work that he did in the United States Senate.

102
00:11:44,140 --> 00:11:47,320
I would love for Senator Harkin to join me up here on the stage for a moment.

103
00:12:22,190 --> 00:12:32,370
I know that for far too long DC has been broken, that the Senate has been broken, but but I believe to my core that the United States Senate is the single

104
00:12:32,370 --> 00:12:35,050
Greatest vehicle to make societal change.

105
00:12:35,050 --> 00:12:40,390
And I believe that ability for a a good senator to change lives.

106
00:12:40,790 --> 00:12:44,570
I've seen it because one senator changed mine.

107
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:55,854
When I was 11 years old, when I was 11 years old, disabled boy living in Council Bluffs Iowa,

108
00:12:56,720 --> 00:13:04,886
The great Tom Harkin changed my life and gave me and so many other disabled Americans an on-ramp to society.

109
00:13:04,886 --> 00:13:16,590
Had it not been for this man who represents the epitome of what is good and what is good in public service,

110
00:13:17,170 --> 00:13:19,650
My life would have looked very very different.

111
00:13:21,279 --> 00:13:34,000
One one senator's ability to work across the aisle and pass good public policy changed my life.

112
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:42,140
And for 30 years, he represented Iowa and fought for the working class, the small businesses, the small family farms.

113
00:13:42,420 --> 00:13:49,160
He fought for the little guy, the same people I am fighting for, those that cannot afford to make a political donation.

114
00:13:50,060 --> 00:13:50,940
Thank you, sir.

115
00:13:54,520 --> 00:14:02,820
For 448 days, I have said it is going to be beautifully poetic when the man who takes back Senator Harkin's seat is only there because of his work.

116
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:11,112
Well, Iowa, tonight we made history, and we wrote beautiful poetry.

117
00:14:13,424 --> 00:14:18,049
Thank you.

118
00:14:18,940 --> 00:14:23,870
Now, can everyone in my family come join me?

119
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:27,700
I would like to bring my family up here.

120
00:15:01,290 --> 00:15:11,269
You got a big family.

121
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:13,700
I got a big family and a tall family.

122
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:23,360
So to each and every person that knocked doors, made phone calls, donated money, put up a sign,

123
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:27,100
And most importantly entrusted me with your vote.

124
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:28,740
Genuinely, thank you.

125
00:15:29,420 --> 00:15:31,620
I want to thank everyone that has supported me.

126
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:37,390
To my wife, my family, my friends.

127
00:15:37,890 --> 00:15:41,190
Thank you all for your support and thank you all for believing in me.

128
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:52,640
To my staff, our volunteers who put their lives on pause because they believed in what we were doing.

129
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:55,200
From the bottom of my heart, thank you.

130
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:05,020
Tonight, Iowa, we have done something truly historic, and I am proud to be your senator elect.

131
00:16:13,090 --> 00:16:16,170
And now the real work begins.

132
00:16:16,790 --> 00:16:20,230
And together we are going to change this state and change our country.

133
00:16:20,630 --> 00:16:21,630
God bless Iowa.

134
00:16:22,150 --> 00:16:23,070
God bless you all.

135
00:16:23,350 --> 00:16:26,250
And God bless the greatest country on the earth, United States of America.

136
00:16:26,490 --> 00:16:27,010
Thank you all.

137
00:16:29,061 --> 00:16:34,946
Thanks everybody.

138
00:16:34,956 --> 00:16:40,040
USA.